      "claim": "One mouse study reported only limited BBB penetration for compound 1, but the compound still entered the brain after IP administration, so this does not prove inadequate CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple direct in vivo records across rats, mice, baboons, and monkeys consistently show brain penetration, brain:plasma ratios around or above 1, PET uptake, and receptor occupancy. The single limited-penetration record still demonstrates brain entry, so the overall evidence supports meaningful CNS access.",
